course: dictionary
lesson: 1617
title: Long words and short forms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long, like chemotherapy. You can often understand a long word by looking for a short form and reading the clues around it. «Chemo, short for chemotherapy, is strong medicine that kills cancer cells» tells you that chemo is the short form and chemotherapy is the full name.
explain: The sentence also gives you clues about meaning. Strong medicine that kills cancer cells is a treatment, so chemotherapy is a medical treatment for cancer. Ask yourself what would fit here, then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
explain: This is a serious health topic. If a word or sentence worries you, ask a grown-up you trust to explain it.
fact: Chemotherapy is a treatment for cancer that uses strong medicines.
fact: «Chemo» is a short form of chemotherapy, and people often use it in everyday talk.
fact: Chemotherapy kills fast-growing cells, so hair often falls out during treatment, and it usually grows back afterwards.
fact: Chemotherapy can make people very tired, and this can last for months.
fact: A short form keeps the same meaning as the full word, so chemo and chemotherapy mean the same thing.
exercise: «Chemo, short for chemotherapy, is strong medicine that kills cancer cells.» What does chemo mean? | A type of haircut | A holiday by the sea | *A short form of chemotherapy, a treatment for cancer | Cake baked for a party
exercise: «Chemotherapy kills fast-growing cells, including cancer cells and hair cells, so hair often falls out.» Why does hair often fall out? | Because hair dislikes sunshine | *Because chemotherapy also kills fast-growing hair cells | Because the medicine is cold | Because the hair is too long
exercise: «Chemo is strong medicine.» Find and copy the short form of chemotherapy. | is | *chemo | medicine | strong
test: «It can make people very tired and sick for months, and many people recover.» What does recover mean here? | Forget the medicine | Get more tired | Go on holiday | *Get better again
test: «Chemotherapy kills fast-growing cells, so hair usually grows back after treatment.» What does usually mean? | Very quickly | Never | *Most of the time | Only once
exam: «In September 2024 she finished chemotherapy, and later she was in remission, meaning there was no sign of the cancer for now.» What does remission mean here? | Feeling very tired | A long holiday | A new kind of medicine | *No sign of the cancer for now
